Inspirations
------------

No code, artwork or audio was taken from any of these.

RIAA playback equalisation
  The 3180, 318 and 75 microsecond time constants are the published
  standard for microgroove records.

Thorens TD 115 MK II (1981 to 1984)
  The 3D deck is a model of this turntable, built from published
  specifications and from photographs used as reference (docs/REFERENCE.md).
  The THORENS wordmark and "TD 115 MKII" appear on the model as they appear on
  the real deck: the wordmark is traced as vector paths from a photograph, the
  model lettering is set in Inter. Thorens is a trademark of its owner. This
  project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Thorens.

Realistic Vinyl Player and its single-file edition, by Lucas Van De Weerd
  The two projects this one succeeds (same author, MIT). Their code was copied
  and adapted: the audio engine, worklet, library, queue and controls of the
  app, and the record model, cut-record chain, wear, tag parsers, demo tracks
  and self-test of the single file.

henryjeff/portfolio-website
  Its technique and discipline (one continuous 3D world, a slow camera, custom
  shaders, restrained post-processing) guided the approach. The repository
  has no licence, so nothing was taken from it: no code, content, layout or
  palette.
  https://github.com/henryjeff/portfolio-website

Vinyl-Player by Lucas Van De Weerd (Gitguy268)
  The author's earlier single-file player. Its colour palette, compact
  controls, glow ring, tone controls, colour pickers and Record Info panel
  were reimplemented here; no code was copied.
  https://github.com/Gitguy268/Vinyl-Player

Winampify (MIT)
  The library desktop, where artists and albums are folders and tracks are
  files to drag onto the player, follows its idea. No code was taken.
  https://github.com/remigallego/winampify

awesome-audio-visualization (CC0)
  The Lines (ridgeline), Oscilloscope, Spectrogram and Radial label
  visualizers are ideas found through this list, among them its "Lines"
  experiment and the "Awesome Audio Player" and "CircleLineNERDDISCO" pens.
  They are drawn from scratch; no code was taken from the list's entries.
  https://github.com/willianjusten/awesome-audio-visualization

Classic VU meters
  The 300 ms needle ballistics follow the traditional VU specification.

